4},{"w":"didn't","start":294.664},{"w":"exist.","start":295.104},{"w":"The","start":295.744},{"w":"lawyers","start":296.064},{"w":"filed","start":296.624},{"w":"them","start":296.984},{"w":"anyway,","start":297.184},{"w":"and","start":297.664},{"w":"the","start":297.784},{"w":"court","start":297.944},{"w":"fined","start":298.264},{"w":"them","start":298.544},{"w":"five","start":298.704},{"w":"thousand","start":299.064},{"w":"dollars.","start":299.504}]}],"title":"AI blooper: cases that never existed","shortTitle":"AI blooper: cases that never existed","props":{"year":2023,"label":"MADE-UP COURT CASES","quoted":false,"token":"Varghese v. China Southern Airlines","explain":"Lawyers filed a brief citing cases a chatbot invented. The court fined them $5,000.","prompt":"Find past cases that support my client's claim…","reply":"Varghese v. China Southern Airlines, 2019…","replyAt":"c32@reply"},"start":275.667,"end":300.04,"startFrame":8270,"durationInFrames":759},{"id":"myth","kind":"myth","component":"MythVsReality","short":true,"cues":[{"id":"c40","start":300.967,"end":302.477,"marks":{},"text":"Myth versus reality.","words":[{"w":"Myth","start":301.26},{"w":"versus","start":301.554},{"w":"reality.","start":301.847}]},{"id":"c41","start":302.877,"end":306.996,"marks":{},"text":"The myth: a chatbot looks the answer up in a giant database of facts.","words":[{"w":"The","start":302.877},{"w":"myth:","start":303.077},{"w":"a","start":303.477},{"w":"chatbot","start":303.897},{"w":"looks","start":304.317},{"w":"the","start":304.557},{"w":"answer","start":304.717},{"w":"up","start":305.037},{"w":"in","start":305.197},{"w":"a","start":305.317},{"w":"giant","start":305.437},{"w":"database","start":305.897},{"w":"of","start":306.357},{"w":"facts.","start":306.557}]},{"id":"c42","start":307.396,"end":318.661,"marks":{"reality":307.556},"text":"The reality: there is no database of answers inside the model. Each token is predicted fresh, from patterns it learned in training. That's 